#!/usr/bin/env bitcpy

[
  In a loop, reads 1 byte from stdin and then writes the same byte to stdout.
  If the read fails, exits with exit code 0. Ignores write errors.

  The intent is that, when the stream ends, the `end_of_stream` error
  will be returned from the read syscall, meaning we are done reading.
  However, this will also exit successfully if a different error occurs.
]

[ .00000000 ] 02200000 00000000 00000000 0a000000 80000000

[ data ]
[ .0a000000 ] 00000000 [ buffer to read/write (only first byte is used) ]
[ .0c000000 ] 00000000 00000000 [ read syscall number and stdin fd ]
[ .00100000 ] 10000000 10000000 [ write syscall number and stdout fd ]
[ .04100000 ] c3000000 00000000 [ exit syscall number and exit code 0 ]
[ .08100000 ] 06100000 0e200000 [ jump locations   0: loop start  1: exit ]

[ main function ]
[ the program will start at the second instruction ]
[ .0c100000 ] 00100000 02000000 04000000 [ write to stdout ]
[ .02200000 ] 0c000000 02000000 04000000 [ read from stdin ]
[ .08200000 ] f3000000 5e200000 10000000 [ set source of next instruction to error bit of read ]
[ .0e200000 ] 08100000 00000000 02000000 [ jump to loop start or exit based on error bit ]
[ .04300000 ] 04100000 02000000 04000000 [ exit ]
